  "statement": "Signer-side anonymization, trust model A: the issuing CA's P-256 key (a public input) signed, with ECDSA-SHA256, a certificate whose P-256 subject key (pinned inside the signed TBSCertificate) signed the manifest-stripped asset digest (a public input), and the certificate's validity period (also pinned) contains a prover-chosen timestamp (a public input the verifier does not check). Off-circuit, the issuing CA chain in x5chain is validated against a trust list.",
  "accounting": "one_time = compile + setup (per circuit and keys). anonymization_per_asset = prepare + witness + prove + package: the complete latency of anonymizing one asset, from a signed asset to an anonymized one, excluding one-time work; anonymization_witness_plus_prove is the subtotal for proof generation alone. verification = loading and preparing the verifying key and verifying the proof; verification_full = the verifier CLI on the anonymized asset (trust-list chain validation, assertion and digest checks, and the proof). test_fixture (generating the test PKI and signing the sample asset) is not part of any total. Peak memory per category is the maximum over its phases, each a separate process.",
